+## The coupled global run (ModflowGPU T5.5b)
+
+Everything north of 60°N is masked out in both models (ModflowGPU PLAN.md decision 10):
+
+- `make_60N_inputs.jl <outdir>` writes the derived inputs (new files, the originals are
+  unchanged): mGV's parameter file with `run_cell` = 0 north of 60°N, MODFLOW's ibound and
+  land mask with 0 north of 60°N (no-flow at the cut), and the provided steady head with
+  sea level (0 m) on the CHD ring. It prints the mask counts, the routing links cut, the
+  shortest remaining channel and the DEM check of the CHD heads. On this machine
+  `<outdir>` is `/home/bart/data/mGV/global_60N`.
+- `global_60N.toml` and `mgv_global_60N.toml`: the configs of the run.
+- `run_global.jl`: the coupled spin-up (`mode=spinup`; the 1979 forcing cycled, checkpoints
+  every `segment` years, stopping criterion) and timed daily runs from a checkpoint
+  (`mode=daily`). The river loss is limited to the water in mGV's channels
+  (`river_water_volume`, `Coupling(...; limit_river_loss = true)`).
+- `compare_indus.jl <heads.nc>`: the Indus cut of global heads against the Indus steady
+  states in `INDUS_DATA`.
+
