+# Fraction of the channel volume a river cell may lose in one stress period when the
+# river-loss limit applies (`river_bottom`): slightly below 1, so the rounding of the
+# fluxes (engine precision) and of the land-surface model's update (Float32) cannot take
+# more than the channel holds.
+const RIVER_LOSS_FRACTION = 0.999
+
+"""
+    river_bottom(stage, bottom, conductance, volume, days, fraction)
+
+RIV bottom (MF6 RBOT) that limits the river loss to the water in the channel (ModflowGPU
+T5.5b): a RIV cell loses at most `conductance · (stage − rbot)` per day (when the head
+is below `rbot`), so `rbot = stage − fraction · volume / (conductance · days)`
+(`fraction = RIVER_LOSS_FRACTION`)
+bounds the loss over the period by the channel volume, whatever the head. The bottom is
+only raised (`max` with `bottom`), never above the stage, and only where the stage lies
+above it; gains (head above the stage) are not changed. `volume = Inf` (no channel volume
+set) or a zero conductance gives `bottom`: no limit, the records are as before.
+"""
+@inline function river_bottom(stage, bottom, conductance, volume, days, fraction)
+    (stage > bottom && conductance > 0 && isfinite(volume)) || return bottom
+    return max(bottom, stage - fraction * volume / (conductance * days))
+end
 
